    "body": "Is this a behavior change? (Parsing relative to document's URL straight-up, instead of the override (or \"about base URL\" in today's parlance).\n\nI guess if I:\n - Create a base element with an `href=/foo` attribute\n - Create an about:blank iframe\n - Check `document.body.baseURI; // resolves to /foo` in the iframe\n - Create a base element in the iframe with an `href=/bar` attribute\n - Check `document.body.baseURI; // resolves to /bar` in the iframe, not `/foo/bar`\n\nChrome agrees with this (haven't checked other browsers). So I guess this aligns the spec to match browsers here?",
