    "body": "> I guess you meant foo and not `/foo`?\r\n\r\nNo, in my testing I used `/foo`. Both worked the same.\r\n\r\n> And `/bar/` instead of `/bar`?\r\n\r\nSame answer as above, but maybe that's buggy.\r\n\r\n> But this is a case where we change behavior to make cloning work well, ensure cloning is idempotent\r\n\r\nYeah I don't oppose the change. I just noticed it doesn't match Safari and Chrome, so should we file implementation bugs and link them to the OP? Here's what I was testing with this particular case (using `foo` and `/bar/`):\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// Step 1:\r\nconst base = document.createElement('base');\r\nbase.href = 'foo';\r\ndocument.head.append(base);\r\n\r\n// Step 2:\r\nconst iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\r\ndocument.body.append(iframe);\r\n\r\n// Step 3:\r\nconsole.log(iframe.contentDocument.baseURI);\r\n\r\n// Step 4:\r\nconst innerBase = iframe.contentDocument.createElement('base');\r\ninnerBase.href = '/bar/';\r\niframe.contentDocument.head.append(innerBase);\r\n\r\n// Step 5:\r\nconsole.log(iframe.contentDocument.baseURI);\r\n```",
