    "body": "> Oh yes, I need to file implementation bugs still. If you could file one for Chromium that'd be good as I keep hitting an extremely annoying captcha.\r\n\r\nI can, but can you clarify what captcha you're seeing? And are you unable to solve it? Is this just right on https://crbug.com/new?\r\n\r\n> I think I mistyped above, but your example also does not make a lot of sense to me still. If you have both `/foo` and `/bar`, how could you ever expect to end up at `/foo/bar`?\r\n\r\nWho said I was trying to end up at `/foo/bar`? I was trying to show that the iframe's base parses against the document's URL, `about:blank` and is thus unresolvable, as opposed to parsing with the document's base URL incorporated.\r\n\r\nActually in that case, Chrome does _not_ follow the spec in which case my statement above:\r\n\r\n> Chrome agrees with this (haven't checked other browsers).\r\n\r\n... is wrong. That's fine, I just want to make sure I understand the behavior change here.",
